Web design prices in Merthyr Tydfil — and across the Valleys generally — vary more than most business owners expect. You can find someone quoting £250, and you can find agencies quoting £5,000 for what looks like the same brief. The difference matters.

Here's a clear breakdown of what web design actually costs for a Merthyr Tydfil business and what you should get at each level.

## What drives the cost?

**How many pages you need** — A four-page starter site for a sole trader costs less than a fifteen-page service site with galleries, testimonials, and a contact system. The scope of the project directly drives the price.

**Custom design vs adapted template** — A designer building your site from scratch charges more than one adapting a pre-bought theme. Custom work produces a site that's unique to your business. Template work produces a site that could belong to anyone.

**SEO** — Not every designer includes on-page SEO as standard. A Merthyr website that doesn't show up in Google searches for CF47 or "near Merthyr" terms is not doing its job. Ask what's included.

**Who's doing it** — An agency with multiple layers and overheads charges more than a local independent designer. That overhead doesn't always mean a better result.

**Ongoing costs** — Domain, hosting, maintenance, and support add to the total cost of ownership. Understand the full picture before committing.

## Merthyr Tydfil web design price ranges

**From £199 — One-page WordPress starter site**

This is where NC Digital's entry-level builds sit. A focused one-page WordPress website is not a generic template. It's a well-built site using the right tools, designed to load fast, look professional, and give your business a credible online presence.

This level suits Merthyr sole traders and small businesses that need a credible, functional website without a large upfront cost.

**£800–£2,500 — Independent designer / small studio**

A fully custom-designed website built around your specific business, with proper SEO foundations and direct communication throughout. Most Merthyr Tydfil businesses investing in a quality website sit in this range.

**£2,500+ — Complex or larger projects**

[Ecommerce](/services/ecommerce-development/), booking systems, multiple service areas, larger content-heavy sites. The cost reflects genuine extra work — but make sure you actually need those features before committing to this budget.

## The monthly option — from £20/month inc. VAT

If a large upfront payment isn't practical, our [Managed Starter Website](/services/managed-starter-websites/) gives Merthyr businesses a fully managed, professionally built website from £20/month inc. VAT. That includes domain, hosting, management, small changes, and 5, 10, or unlimited new pages added each month depending on your tier.

For most Merthyr tradespeople and small businesses, one new customer from your website covers months of that cost.

## The cheapest option is rarely the best value

A website that doesn't show up on Google, doesn't turn visitors into enquiries, or needs rebuilding within a year is not a saving — it's a more expensive problem. The right question isn't "how little can I spend?" It's "what's the cost of a website that actually works?"

